        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px"><a href="backbox">BackBox</a> Linux, an Ubuntu-based distribution used to perform penetration tests and security assessments, has been updated to version 10. This major new release is based on Ubuntu 26.04. "<span class="Quote">The BackBox team is happy to announce the new major release of BackBox Linux, version 10. As usual, this major release includes many updates. These include a new kernel, new and updated tools and some structural changes, with a focus on maintaining stability and compatibility with Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. What's new: updated Linux kernel 7.0; updated desktop environment (Xfce 4.20); updated hacking tools, including Metasploit Framework 6.5, Nmap 7.98, Wireshark 4.6, sqlmap 1.10, hashcat 7.1 and ZAP 2.17; new tools - ffuf and gobuster for web content discovery, AFL++ for fuzzing, GDB, LLDB, ltrace and checksec for binary analysis, Samba client and the Kerberos and LDAP clients for Windows and Active Directory networks, plus hashID, mdk4, Firejail, apksigner and aapt; reworked anonymous mode - DNS queries now go through Tor as well, IPv6 is blocked while it is active, and anonymous stop restores the original network settings; better VMware support....</span>" The <a href="https://blog.backbox.org/2026/11/19/backbox-linux-10-released/">release announcement</a> also lists system requirements. <a href="https://linux.backbox.org/download/">Download (SHA256)</a>: <a href="https://mirror.backbox.org/backbox-10-desktop-amd64.iso">backbox-10-desktop-amd64.iso</a> (6,119MB, <a href="https://mirror.backbox.org/backbox-10-desktop-amd64.iso.torrent">torrent</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=backbox&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=9#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
